{"author":{"id":"85a3c31a64931f83958f26b24045fef8415ea6ff04d942d15661891c77fc0695"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794223160,"nonce":"c8aAn1RZMq4GILH9bV/IfsXHPn8=","message":"Working tree (uncommitted, russl/toy, its own workspace): a Blinc app laid out as an editor workbench. The sketch's modules are tabs (main is the root, others import by name, use crate::\u003ctab\u003e::f), each editor in JetBrains Mono (bundled, OFL) through the stylesheet's --blinc-code-font-family, highlighted by russl's own highlighters (russl, WGSL, MSL, HLSL, GLSL), on the theme's surface. Every edit recompiles all modules; problems show inline in the module they are in (Blinc's new set_code_diagnostics), as rows in the panel's Problems tab (icon, message, module [line, col], a click reveals it), and as counts in the status bar. Beside the editor: the live preview (Blinc flow pipeline) and a collapsible inspector of the pipeline constants (cn switch and number gauge, re-specialised on change) and the bindings. Below: Problems and each target's output in tabs, beside a console logging compiles. Splits are cn resizable groups; panel and inspector fold from the status bar. Tested offscreen with blinc_recorder: the starter sketch draws, the panel folds, and a two-module sketch with an error in one and a warning in the other shows each where it belongs. Depends on unreleased Blinc (inline diagnostics, --blinc-code-font-family); the git rev moves once that lands.","files":null}]}